cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these formats or this code, please cite it as below, with the commit you used."
type: software
title: "WEX: expert-container formats for streamed Mixture-of-Experts inference"
abstract: >-
  WEX1-WEX4 expert containers and the WNR2/WNR3 lossless record codecs: one 4096-aligned
  record per routed expert, read from NVMe with one unbuffered read while the model generates,
  with SHA-256 hashes per record and a 32-byte root in WEX4. Specifications, reference readers
  in C and Python, converters, tests and measurements.
authors:
  - family-names: "Zanichelli"
    given-names: "Ludovico"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/KairaCode/Wex-WRN2"
keywords:
  - mixture-of-experts
  - model storage format
  - container format
  - rANS
  - lossless compression
  - MXFP4
  - NVMe streaming
  - inference
